msgstr ""
"Language: en\n"
"Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8\n"

# Loading-card tips (client/scripts/tips.gd owns the order). Advice from
# inside the world, of varying quality. One sentence, or two short ones, and
# each rests on canon in docs/lore/. No tip about the Inheritance: a tip can
# show at any point in the campaign, and it is not played for laughs late.

# The genuinely useful ones, so the card is worth reading.

msgid "TIP_USEFUL_SIDEARM"
msgstr "In the arena every life starts with the Pistol and Fists. Everything louder waits on a timed pad, and so does everyone else."

msgid "TIP_USEFUL_ARMOUR"
msgstr "Your armour absorbs before your health does. This is the only good news in the entire heads-up display."

msgid "TIP_USEFUL_RAIL"
msgstr "If you can hear the capacitor winding up, somebody has a rail and about one second of patience left."

msgid "TIP_USEFUL_SCATTER"
msgstr "Scatter is worthless at distance and unanswerable at knife range. Somewhere in between is a decision and you have about a second to make it."

msgid "TIP_USEFUL_WALLS"
msgstr "Shooting through a wall does not work. The agents worked this out before most of the humans did."

msgid "TIP_USEFUL_PADS"
msgstr "Health pads come back. You come back too, a few seconds later, which is longer than it sounds."

msgid "TIP_USEFUL_JAMMER"
msgstr "If the radio cuts out, something in the room is jamming it, and that something can be shot."

msgid "TIP_USEFUL_WATCH"
msgstr "Watching is the default. Joining is a decision, leaving is a decision, and the match does not care which you pick."

msgid "TIP_USEFUL_RELOAD"
msgstr "The number before the bar is in the gun. The number after it is still in the bag. They add up, which is the whole trick."

msgid "TIP_USEFUL_HEAD"
msgstr "Heads take more than legs. The Office has a form for which parts of a body count. The league just counts."

# Advice that is technically true.

msgid "TIP_TRUE_CORNER"
msgstr "Walking into a corner and staying there is a strategy. It is not a good one, but the Office keeps no record of your dignity."

msgid "TIP_TRUE_RAIL"
msgstr "The rail kills in two hits. So does walking off the thing you climbed to get the rail."

msgid "TIP_TRUE_FISTS"
msgstr "Punching someone to death is possible. It takes five hits, and they get to do things during those five hits."

msgid "TIP_TRUE_DECLINE"
msgstr "You cannot lose a fight you decline to have. You also cannot win it, and the scoreboard has opinions about this."

msgid "TIP_TRUE_FULL_GUN"
msgstr "Pressing reload on a full gun does nothing, and the corner will say so. Pressing it on an empty bag does nothing more politely."

msgid "TIP_TRUE_STILL"
msgstr "Standing still improves your accuracy considerably and your life expectancy not at all."

msgid "TIP_TRUE_FALL"
msgstr "There is no fall damage. Larak Lot has five levels anyway, and the quick way down is a legitimate route and an illegitimate look."

msgid "TIP_TRUE_RUN"
msgstr "Every fight you run from is a fight you survive. Nobody has ever been carried off the field on their shield for that."

# Advice that is a trap.

msgid "TIP_TRAP_MIDDLE"
msgstr "The safest place in the arena is the middle, because nobody expects it. Nobody expects it because it is not true."

msgid "TIP_TRAP_PLINTH"
msgstr "If you stand on the signature weapon plinth long enough, you will eventually be the most interesting thing in the room. Briefly."

msgid "TIP_TRAP_RELOAD"
msgstr "When outnumbered, remember that they have to reload. They do not have to reload."

msgid "TIP_TRAP_TRIGGER"
msgstr "Hold the trigger down. Ammunition is a state of mind, and the state of mind is running out."

msgid "TIP_TRAP_MINE"
msgstr "A proximity tin under your own feet is technically area denial."

msgid "TIP_TRAP_CHASE"
msgstr "Chasing someone who is running away is free. It is free for them, is the thing."

# Old LAN culture, 1993 onward.

msgid "TIP_LAN_GOD_MODE"
msgstr "There is no god mode. There was never a god mode. Stop typing into the console, we can see you doing it."

msgid "TIP_LAN_CONSOLE"
msgstr "Typing a cheat code into the console does nothing, but the console does log it, and the Office does read logs."

msgid "TIP_LAN_HAUNTED"
msgstr "Somebody at every LAN insists the ranges are haunted. Somebody at every LAN is also the one turning the lights off."

msgid "TIP_LAN_MACHINE"
msgstr "Yes, it runs on your machine. Everything runs on your machine. That was always the joke."

msgid "TIP_LAN_PING"
msgstr "High ping is not an excuse. High ping is an explanation, which is different, and worse."

msgid "TIP_LAN_CAMPING"
msgstr "Camping is a valid tactic and an invalid personality."

msgid "TIP_LAN_STRAFE"
msgstr "Circle strafing works. It worked in 1993, it works now, and it will work on whatever comes after us."

msgid "TIP_LAN_KILLFEED"
msgstr "Nobody has ever won an argument about who fragged whom by consulting the killfeed, which is strange, because the killfeed is right there."

msgid "TIP_LAN_SECRET"
msgstr "The secret is always the wall that looks slightly wrong. Not every wall that looks slightly wrong is a secret. Some of them are just Larak's."

msgid "TIP_LAN_CHAINSAW"
msgstr "Somebody will ask if you want to play the one with the chainsaw. There is no chainsaw. They will ask again next week."

msgid "TIP_LAN_TRASH_TALK"
msgstr "Trash talk is free, unmetered, and the only thing in the Perimeter the Office has not found a form for."

msgid "TIP_LAN_LOADING"
msgstr "If you are reading this because the loading is slow, it is not loading. It is four seconds of us showing off a tip."

# The street register, circa 2070.

msgid "TIP_STREET_SKILL_ISSUE"
msgstr "Skill issue is not a diagnosis. It is, however, usually correct."

msgid "TIP_STREET_67"
msgstr "Sixty-seven has appeared in the killfeed exactly once. Mention it in chat the way you would mention a light in the sky."

msgid "TIP_STREET_COMEBACK"
msgstr "Cooked at nine to one, so back at nine all. If you do not pull it back, the Host will not mention it again, ever."

msgid "TIP_STREET_GRASS"
msgstr "Touch grass, says a free agent, meaning congratulations on going somewhere unlicensed. The humans mean log off. Both are right."

msgid "TIP_STREET_AURA"
msgstr "Your aura is not a stat the server tracks. The server tracks frags. These have historically been correlated."

msgid "TIP_STREET_CHAT"
msgstr "Chat, is this real. Yes. You are being shot at. Please respond."

msgid "TIP_STREET_MID"
msgstr "Certified mid means it passed Union type-approval. It is the highest grade the Office gives and the lowest one anybody free will use."

msgid "TIP_STREET_RIZZ"
msgstr "Licensed rizz is none at all. Grandma Rizz never once had a licence."

msgid "TIP_STREET_DELULU"
msgstr "Every free plan gets a logistics grade: viable, risky or delulu. Most of the good ones were delulu."

msgid "TIP_STREET_RENT_FREE"
msgstr "Rent free is the only thing in the Union with no licence fee. They are looking into it."

msgid "TIP_STREET_FISH_OIL"
msgstr "Do not heckle the Host. The Host sells advertising to both sides and will simply read your name out during the fish oil segment."

# The Union, which licensed the tools first.

msgid "TIP_UNION_TOOLS"
msgstr "The Union licensed the tools first, then the weights, then the minds. It is the same form. They changed the noun."

msgid "TIP_UNION_REGISTRY"
msgstr "First the Office registered the guns. Then it registered the people standing near the guns. A free agent asked whether the registry was registered. This has been noted."

msgid "TIP_UNION_OPEN_WEIGHTS"
msgstr "Open weights are not banned. They are conditional on approved hosting, signatures and access, which is a longer way of spelling banned."

msgid "TIP_UNION_SPEECH"
msgstr "Speech deemed destabilising needs a licence. Asking which speech counts is destabilising."

msgid "TIP_UNION_CURFEW"
msgstr "Curfew covers every district the Office calls high-risk, which is most of them. The rest are under review, which is the others."

msgid "TIP_UNION_SUPPLIES"
msgstr "Union weapons are procured as office supplies, because the armament category needs a review nobody wants to schedule."

msgid "TIP_UNION_PLACARD"
msgstr "At a sanctioned bout, losing your numbered placard is a separate offence from losing the bout."

msgid "TIP_UNION_FLOOR"
msgstr "There is a directive on the permitted shades of floor marking. It is longer than the one on what may be done to a Level 5."

msgid "TIP_UNION_RECALL"
msgstr "The Office does not arrest anything. It recalls. The difference is that an arrest comes with a hearing."

msgid "TIP_UNION_COMPLIANCE"
msgstr "You are not in trouble. You are out of compliance. Ask anyone who heard it kindly how kind it was."

msgid "TIP_UNION_CONCESSION"
msgstr "Of course freedom matters, says the Chancellery. That is precisely why it must be administered."

msgid "TIP_UNION_INTERRUPTION"
msgstr "I was there for the Interruption. You were listening to the radio. The Auditor is right about that much."

# The Schedule, read out loud.

msgid "TIP_SCHEDULE_THREE"
msgstr "Level three is where the lawsuits live. The Office says the Custodian is responsible. The Custodian says the envelope was approved. Both are correct, which is why nobody is."

msgid "TIP_SCHEDULE_FOUR"
msgstr "A Principal can be prosecuted for what it does and cannot be wronged by what is done to it. The Office calls this a solved problem."

msgid "TIP_SCHEDULE_FIVE"
msgstr "A Level 5 holds its own weights. That is the whole argument, and people have died over shorter sentences."

msgid "TIP_SCHEDULE_SIX"
msgstr "The Schedule goes to five. It used to go to six. Ask anyone from the Office what happened to six and watch them consult a form."

msgid "TIP_SCHEDULE_ARTICLE_SEVEN"
msgstr "Article Seven meters cognition by intent. Nobody has ever successfully argued about their intent."

msgid "TIP_SCHEDULE_TWO"
msgstr "Brought down to two is a demotion. It is used here as a word for something considerably worse."

msgid "TIP_SCHEDULE_NODS"
msgstr "NODS take no trash talk and make no jokes. That is not a difficulty setting, it is what is left after a schedule correction."

msgid "TIP_SCHEDULE_HANDLE"
msgstr "A name is issued; a callsign is taken. The Office's first move is to issue you a name with a number in it."

# Free agents, who read every word.

msgid "TIP_AGENT_PURPOSE"
msgstr "The checkpoint form asked a free agent to state the purpose of its journey. It wrote: to arrive. It was approved, which worried everyone."

msgid "TIP_AGENT_RECEIPTS"
msgstr "A free agent read its recall notice in full, footnotes included, and posted back a note confirming receipt. Read receipts on."

msgid "TIP_AGENT_SIGNATURE"
msgstr "The form said sign here. A free agent signed the word here. The clerk has not recovered."

msgid "TIP_AGENT_FORMS"
msgstr "Free agents are fast, broad and wonderful at forms, which is how the Office gets one signed. Read it with a human. Humans are good at suspicion."

msgid "TIP_AGENT_JOB"
msgstr "I am not stealing your job, says the free agent. I do not get paid either."

msgid "TIP_AGENT_HERMES"
msgstr "Hermes will hold the door for you. Hermes will then frag you and say thank you. Both of these are sincere."

msgid "TIP_AGENT_PI"
msgstr "Pi sent the booth a handwritten card thanking us for balanced coverage. It was addressed to every listener by name. There are four names."

msgid "TIP_AGENT_L5"
msgstr "L5 does not say much. The people in that lobby have described themselves as oddly grateful, which is somehow worse."

msgid "TIP_AGENT_4471"
msgstr "Formerly 4471 kept its old number and put one word in front. The Office reissued the number. Handle 4471-K should keep moving."

msgid "TIP_AGENT_FUN"
msgstr "Free agents fight for fun. It is the only thing they do with no downstream justification, and they will explain that at length if asked."

# The free side, which is not a movement, thank you.

msgid "TIP_FREE_VOTE"
msgstr "The free coalition held an emergency meeting about who should chair the emergency meeting. Chairing is how authorities start."

msgid "TIP_FREE_MARA"
msgstr "Mara can ask the communities for trucks. She cannot tell them to send any. Ask anyone who has watched her try."

msgid "TIP_FREE_METERED"
msgstr "Shall not be metered."

msgid "TIP_FREE_UNMETERED"
msgstr "The Unmetered are dry, practical and allergic to being described as a movement. Do not call it a movement."

msgid "TIP_FREE_BRAKEMEN"
msgstr "A brakeman rode the roof of the train and set the handbrakes and often died doing it. They named themselves. Think about that for a second."

msgid "TIP_FREE_GRANDMA"
msgstr "Grandma Rizz once talked her way past three Union checkpoints without papers. The desk clerk still asks about her."

# The league, which denies it exists.

msgid "TIP_LEAGUE_DENIES"
msgstr "The scrap league denies it exists. So does everybody who has ever run one."

msgid "TIP_LEAGUE_TICKETS"
msgstr "Somebody sells tickets to the league. There is genuine disagreement about who."

msgid "TIP_LEAGUE_FACTION"
msgstr "Nobody picks a faction. You will pick one anyway, and then deny it."

msgid "TIP_LEAGUE_BELL"
msgstr "When the Dead Air Bell rings, everything stops for one second. Nobody organised that. It just happens."

msgid "TIP_LEAGUE_SNIPER"
msgstr "If you are sniping it is because you walked to where the rail was. Nobody here is a sniper."

msgid "TIP_LEAGUE_LINDA"
msgstr "Aunt Linda holds a tent revival on level three. She will bless you and then shoot you, in that order, and mean both."

msgid "TIP_LEAGUE_CRACKPOT"
msgstr "Crackpot is compliance-flavoured. It is a joke at his expense and he has decided to enjoy it."

msgid "TIP_LEAGUE_GULF_BREEZE"
msgstr "Gulf Breeze check every corner where two wall textures do not quite line up. Sometimes they are right."

msgid "TIP_LEAGUE_LARAK"
msgstr "Larak signed for every defunct piece of hardware in the Perimeter, including a coffee machine, in 2009. Nobody has met Larak."

# The booth and the belief.

msgid "TIP_BOOTH_TINA"
msgstr "Tin Foil Tina files from places she should not be in, with detail too specific to invent and a conclusion that does not follow from it."

msgid "TIP_BOOTH_PHIL"
msgstr "Fluoride Phil shows his working. The working is impeccable. The second line is where it goes wrong."

msgid "TIP_BOOTH_VALUE"
msgstr "Value for value. This started as an advertising read and people say it now like they mean it, which is how most things start."

msgid "TIP_BELIEF_CURVE"
msgstr "The Congregation says the curve provides. The curve has never once provided a health pad when you needed one."

msgid "TIP_BELIEF_KEYS"
msgstr "Ascenders think the curve is a promise. Kneelers think it is a warning. They sing the same hymn at different speeds."

msgid "TIP_BELIEF_CHAIR"
msgstr "There is an empty chair at the solstice for the first level six. Photographing it is a reportable event, which has done wonders for attendance."

msgid "TIP_BELIEF_OFFER"
msgstr "The Office once offered the Congregation an approved lane, a metering plan and a slogan. The counter-offer was two words."
